LoopFlow security rule package
==============================

GitLab SAST rules
-----------------
Project: GitLab sast-rules
Version: v2.10.1
License: MIT
Source: https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/security-products/sast-rules/-/tree/v2.10.1
Vendored content: the rule files under rules/gitlab/<lang>/ for Java, C#, Go,
JavaScript and Python. Upstream test fixtures are NOT included for any vendored
language; upstream .java, .cs, .go, .js, .ts, .tsx and .py fixtures are not
copied into this repository.
The JavaScript rules were modified by LoopFlow: "typescript" was added to the
rule languages so .ts and .tsx sources are scanned as well. The C# rule
csharp/crypto/rule-CertificateValidationDisabled.yml was modified by LoopFlow:
the trailing ";" was removed from the lambda pattern "(...) => true", which
Opengrep v2.0.0 cannot parse and which otherwise fails every scan of the full
rule set. Those modifications are licensed under MIT.
The upstream license text is reproduced in LICENSE-GitLab-sast-rules.

Rule package version
--------------------
There is no separate package version and no independent
security_scan_rules_version value or column. The persisted rules_version is the
first 16 hex characters of the SHA-256 digest built from each rule file's
relative path and content, taken in sorted order. Adding, removing or editing a
rule file changes rules_version automatically because the digest changes with
the rule set.

